.nh
.TH "BURROW" "1" "Oct 2026" "burrow 0.1.0-dev" "burrow manual"

.SH NAME
burrow-analyze - interactive disk explorer


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBburrow analyze [path...] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Explore where disk space went.

.PP
Interactive mode navigates a tree (arrow keys) and can move items to the
freedesktop Trash with 'd'/'D'. Read-only otherwise.

.PP
The --json schema is stable:
  {"path":"...","total_size":N,"total_files":N,
   "entries":[{"name":"...","path":"...","size":N,"is_dir":true}],
   "largest":[...],"scan_status":"complete|partial|unavailable"}

.PP
When stdout is not a terminal (or --json is set), analyze behaves like
--json and never waits for input. --json accepts a single path.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-a\fP, \fB--apparent\fP[=false]
	show apparent size instead of on-disk usage

.PP
\fB--depth\fP=0
	non-interactive depth (with --json); 0 = unlimited

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for analyze

.PP
\fB--no-delete\fP[=false]
	disable the 'd'/'D' trash keys (read-only mode)

.PP
\fB-H\fP, \fB--no-hidden\fP[=false]
	skip dotfiles

.PP
\fB-x\fP, \fB--one-file-system\fP[=false]
	do not descend across mount points

.PP
\fB-t\fP, \fB--top\fP=10
	non-interactive top-N largest entries (with --json)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	terminal color policy: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB--config\fP=""
	override the config file path

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	never mutate; print the plan and exit

.PP
\fB--exclude\fP=[]
	comma list of categories or item ids to exclude

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	machine-readable output

.PP
\fB--log-level\fP="info"
	trace|debug|info|warn|error

.PP
\fB--min-size\fP="0"
	only act on items >= size (e.g. 10M, 1G)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable color (same as --color=never)

.PP
\fB--only\fP=[]
	comma list of categories or item ids to include

.PP
\fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	only print errors

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	shorthand for --log-level debug

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	skip the interactive confirm


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBburrow(1)\fP
